{**
 * c-toast - short news drawn over the page in a corner of the window: what
 * came of something just done.
 *
 * It takes the messages the way Nette hands its flash messages over - objects
 * with a message and a type - so that both layouts draw $flashes with it as
 * they are, in the corner of the window (corner: true), inside the snippet the
 * base presenters redraw when an answer to Naja has something to say. A
 * message said before a redirect arrives with the page the redirect leads to;
 * one said in answer to Naja arrives in that snippet, and replaces what was
 * there rather than piling up on it. The type names what kind of news it is,
 * as it does for c-notice: info, or danger for a refusal. A type it does not
 * know stops the page (Argument) rather than being drawn as information: a
 * refusal said with a typing mistake in its type would otherwise be read out
 * as a quiet status and look like good news.
 *
 * **What a screen reader hears** is the sentence and not the toast, for the
 * reason c-notice gives: a live region holding the button would announce
 * "Saved. Dismiss" every time. A refusal is an alert, which interrupts; the
 * rest is a status, which waits its turn. A toast arrives already holding its
 * sentence, and a live region is read when it changes after the reader has
 * seen it, so assets/toast.ts puts the sentence in again once the toast is on
 * the page.
 *
 * **It stays until it is put away.** A toast that went by itself would have to
 * give whoever reads it the time they need, and a pause while the pointer or
 * the focus is on it does not reach somebody who is reading it from elsewhere
 * - zoomed in on another part of the page, or listening to the next thing
 * already - so it would still be gone before some of them had read it (WCAG
 * 2.2.1). What a toast here says is what came of what somebody did, and that
 * is not something to take away on a timer. Its c-close puts it away the way
 * a dismissible c-notice is put away (assets/notice.ts), and the next page, or
 * the next message, replaces it anyway.
 *}

{import 'close.latte'}

{define toast, array $messages, bool $corner = false, ?string $testId = null}
    <div n:if="$messages !== []" n:class="'c-toast', $corner ? 'c-toast--corner'" data-testid="{$testId}">
        {foreach $messages as $toast}{do Trilobit\Core\Presentation\Component\Argument::oneOf('c-toast', 'type', $toast->type, ['info', 'danger'])}{/foreach}
        <div n:foreach="$messages as $toast" n:class="'c-toast__item', $toast->type === 'danger' ? 'c-toast__item--danger'">
            <p class="c-toast__message" role="{$toast->type === 'danger' ? 'alert' : 'status'}">{$toast->message}</p>
            {include close, label: 'Dismiss'}
        </div>
    </div>
{/define}
